WEBVTT

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.830
Pandora's Box is the one you're not supposed to open.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.040
But humans just can't help themselves. When we opened it,

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.340
out came something remarkably similar to Gekiganger.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:17.010
What? I thought this was supposed to be a real-robot anime?

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.890
I wonder where we're going?

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:58.050
It does look like someone was onboard.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.290
But is that possible?

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:02.820
The weapons used by the Jovian Lizards have been unmanned.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.820
And Inez-sensei stated that no ordinary life form can pass through a Chulip.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:08.540
The "Significant Other" from a Star Far Away

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:09.790
Enough jabbering!

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:14.150
In any case, we need to find the enemy pilot who's infiltrated our ship.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.150
This is top secret!

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:15.710
I see.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:17.070
Go right ahead!

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:21.530
Why does the maintenance crew have to do this?

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.110
Why not let Security handle it?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.930
If we did something like that, everyone would find out!

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.450
We'd have a panic on our hands! Absolutely not!

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:33.600
I've had the top brass yell at me, "Keep this under wraps, or else!"

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:38.860
This big oaf wouldn't happen to be the UEAF's new weapon, would it?

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:44.770
Maybe something about collecting data while matching it against our Nadesico?

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.280
Well, that may be the case.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:47.900
Oh, well.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:50.750
We will protect our own ship!

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:51.710
Right!

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.570
Rather surprising.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:59.410
I thought Nergal's policy was to coordinate with the military,

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.860
but here we are allowed to run off to the Moon to welcome back Tenkawa Akito.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:05.140
It seems that they want to exchange crews

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:07.550
with the fourth vessel before it falls under military control.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.670
But in my case, Tenkawa Akito is much more important to me.

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:15.190
Does the secretary to the chairman find his type to be attractive as well?

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:17.820
What was that?!

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.320
I swear! This ship has a bad habit of assuming that relationships between men and women

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.880
always have a romantic twist to them!

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.880
I'm not amused!

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:28.570
I'm only interested in him for his promise as a research subject.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:29.040
Okay?

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.410
It's not okay!

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:31.490
What?

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.470
Please stop doing strange things to Akito!

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.790
If you do, I'll...

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:38.540
Do what?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:39.620
What?

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.050
Hit me? Kick me? Slap me?

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.640
Well...

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.320
But...

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.720
All right.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:46.710
Then you'll...

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:48.880
I'll explain this to you very clearly!

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:49.640
What?

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:52.560
Explain?

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.900
It's faster to show than to explain.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.320
Something happened during your boson jump from Mars to lunar orbit.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:03.150
In other words, the love between Akito and myself brought about a miracle!

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.830
So, Inez-sensei was the interference in our romantic...

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.460
There you are, Ms. Explains Everything.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:09.580
According to his own testimony,

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:14.000
it's very possible Akito-kun successfully boson jumped from Mars to Earth,

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:17.030
making Akito a very special person.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.030
Isn't that right? Oh, excuse me.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:23.040
Yes, that's absolutely right!

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.410
In other words, Akito is a very special person for me!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.380
That's not it!

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:27.780
Okay...

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.260
Being able to explain his abilities

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:33.180
will assist with our research in making organic boson jumping a reality.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.190
With that, we can send sophisticated manned weapons against the Jovian Lizards!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:38.980
The strategic outlook will change dramatically!

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:44.300
Yume ga asu o yonteiru tamashii no sakebi sa

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.030
RETTSU GOO PASSHON

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.840
itsu no hi ka heiwa wo torimodose kono te ni

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.480
Did you spot something?

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:50.040
itsu no hi ka heiwa wo torimodose kono te ni

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:50.710
It's yo...

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:51.260
itsu no hi ka heiwa wo torimodose kono te ni

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:51.460
RETTSU GOO GEKIGANGAA 3

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.790
I can't say I've noticed anything special.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:56.480
Oh, I see...

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:57.960
So, did something come up?

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:01.380
I'm on a top secret mission, so please keep this to yourselves.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.990
I think we want to keep quiet on this.

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:08.220
Was Gekiganger infectious?

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.730
I've finished spreading the stickers on the bridge and the surrounding areas.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:19.600
Behold, a total encirclement setup!

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.010
The pilot appears to be quite a Gekigan-mania.

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.070
He'll jump for it!

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.030
Come whenever you're ready!

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:29.990
Minato...

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:33.950
I'm not getting off duty.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.870
What are you asking me to do?

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.530
Say, what keeps Mr. Goat Hory onboard the Nadesico?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.270
Because it's your job? Because you've been ordered to?

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.420
Was it part of your job to be like this with me?

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:46.780
I'm onboard the Nadesico because that's my job.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.620
I have no grudges against the Jovian Lizards.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.680
So when the war's over, all you want is a happy family awaiting your return?

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.600
I don't want to mix work with personal matters.

00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.030
Then am I part of your private life?

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.450
I don't come to work everyday expecting to protect women.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.320
All systems operating normally.

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.080
Ruri-Ruri, how long have you been here?

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.200
I've been here from the beginning.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.710
Oh, well...

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:21.110
There's nothing to worry about.

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.130
I'm only a young girl. I don't understand adult conversations.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.410
I'll take off now to clean up.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:30.320
Could you cover for me, Ruri-Ruri?

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.040
Sure.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:31.550
Minato!

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.990
What? Is it all over already?

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.710
Baka!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:42.020
You three?!

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:43.970
Hey, don't get us wrong.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.680
We were here taking it easy when this began, and we meant to go but couldn't.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:48.940
We didn't hear anything! Right? Right?

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:56.200
A mixing wok with a secret batter?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.740
Now that's mixing work with personal matters!

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:01.170
Baka...

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:05.540
Please!

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:07.610
He's Rokurou-niisan.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.210
He's my only brother!

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:14.010
But now he is Shi'koos, warrior for the Dark String Universe!

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.700
Nanako-san, he is now the enemy.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:20.710
What's the matter, Gekiganger?!

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:23.990
I'll go ahead then!

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:28.650
Nanako-san...

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:29.780
Ken...

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.120
I'm sorry!

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:32.990
Why?!

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.910
Why do you have to fight amongst yourselves?!

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:37.620
Why?!

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.400
Why?

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.370
Why do you have to fight?!

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.370
There you are, Tenkuu Ken.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:46.930
While I have nothing against you personally,

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:48.450
I can do better.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:48.680
While I have nothing against you personally,

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.020
I must fight you as a warrior of the Kyo'Ak.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:51.860
This is our destiny!

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.050
Hold on a second!

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:56.970
Usa-tan?!

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.680
I was right!

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:03.640
This is the lost episode 13, "The Tragic Holy Night! Satan Clock M!"

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:04.900
How can this be?!

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.520
Women

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.610
I think it's all right.

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.440
You're being honest to yourself as a girl in love.

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.800
Well, that might be fine for some common office worker,

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.980
but you're the captain, right?

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:17.870
Yes, that's right!

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.160
Then what motivates you to be captain of the Nadesico?

00:08:22.840 --> 00:08:26.040
I'm here because I was requested.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:29.240
At home and the university, they only saw me as being my father's daughter,

00:08:29.240 --> 00:08:32.550
the eldest of the Misumaru family, but here I'm somebody,

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:37.340
and I want to continue to serve people for as long as they want me to.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:39.730
Is that it? That's all?

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:43.740
Well, there's that part about capturing Akito's heart,

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:45.350
and jumping right into a romantic, love-love mode!

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.900
I get frustrated, you know, just watching you.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:51.940
You waltz on acting as if being the captain is the norm.

00:08:51.940 --> 00:08:54.530
Everyone pampers you, dismissing you as a figurehead captain.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.040
What have you accomplished anyway?

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:59.700
What have you achieved as captain of this vessel?

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:03.210
I think she's a pretty good captain. She's not oppressive.

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:05.940
But how many people died under her?

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:10.950
It's easy to say "work and romance both matter a lot to me,"

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.800
but that's something only those who can handle the work can stake a claim to.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.250
Are you fulfilling your duties as captain adequately?

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:19.300
In the end, what do you intend to accomplish as captain of the Nadesico?

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:21.550
You can't expect an answer if you hammer away like that.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.850
I don't think the questions that Won-san are posing are unreasonable.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.380
There's nothing wrong with chasing after Akito's love.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:36.480
But I would like to have Ms. Yurika tell us about her specific goals and dreams as captain of the Nadesico.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:40.320
I became the captain during the war.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:45.240
All I can think about is protecting this ship for as long as the war rages on.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.220
But I think it's worthwhile

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:51.040
to think about who best we can enjoy our lives with, even during wartime.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.420
Then what will you do if there is no resolution?

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:00.310
Delicious!

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:03.080
So what I want to say to you is:

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.340
I don't care if you think you're a captain or not,

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:07.990
if you can't figure out what your role in the war is, or your goal at work,

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.720
then all you're doing is playing around.

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:11.600
I don't want someone like that getting in my way.

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:14.770
So, what about you? You got this vision thing?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.280
In three years, I'll make it to the top of Nergal.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.440
Wow...

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.730
To make it to the top of Nergal

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.240
means you are nearly in control of all the major economic interests of Earth.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:25.480
I want to be able to bring about

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:27.080
the full recovery of Earth through my own abilities.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.470
I would also like to win the war.

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:34.420
Well, maybe I don't have the high goals that you do,

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.290
but I want to protect the Nadesico and Akito!

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.840
The Nadesico is where we can all be ourselves.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:41.630
Easier said than done.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.730
Is this all right, Chief?

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.670
We were supposed to be conducting a search.

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:47.840
Just kill me now.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:53.480
You want to kill me?!

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:56.400
But you said you wanted to die right now.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.670
What are you up to, Uripee?

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:01.320
Oh well, actually we're looking for an intruder.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.660
Intruder?

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.700
Is it true a vicious sexual molester is loose and stealing people's underwear?

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:12.330
Is it true that you ordered Uripee to be a Peeping Tom?

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:17.310
instructing the maintenance crew to collect the underwear of men?!

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:17.970
Pervert!

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.800
Would you like me to explain?

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:21.760
Admiral!

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:23.760
Baka...

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.630
Here's your lunar surface tonkatsu combo!

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:33.710
Fried leek and liver, ready!

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:34.570
All right!

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:35.850
Finished with the delivery!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.730
Oh, good work.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:38.970
How was it?

00:11:38.970 --> 00:11:41.010
Were you able to contact that Yamato something?
Note: Yamato Nadesico = Traditional japanese women

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.780
It's not Yamato something. The name is Nadesico. Nadesico!

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.200
Oh, yes. Well, they're on their way here.

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:50.490
Well, that's good. Isn't that great, Aki-bou?

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.850
That's wonderful.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.640
It'll only be a few more days until the chef here isn't bossing you around.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:57.140
Now listen, when did I ever boss him around?

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:59.130
Come on. Come up and get yourself something to eat.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:00.590
There you are!

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.940
After all that, my message didn't make it in time.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:07.500
About that person you wanted to save?

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.560
She died in place of me.

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:12.140
Don't say it like that.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.210
We've been living on the Moon for a while, right?

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:18.510
Well, I've had to watch a lot of people I know pass away.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:22.680
But I never let myself think that the people next door died instead of me.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.610
That only makes the people who did die...

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.870
Well... Well...

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.090
I'm sorry. I know what you mean.

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.560
But that girl died.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.690
For the first week, I was stuck in the hospital.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.360
Then I was interrogated by people from Nergal.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.010
I was thinking all that time.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.560
How was I able to do something like this?

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:43.210
Why am I living the same two weeks again?

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:45.630
If only I could make up my mind a little sooner.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.130
That's why I wanted to start anew.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.530
I could redo everything. That's the reason I came here.

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:53.550
But I couldn't.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.040
I wasn't able to fix what went wrong.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.140
What's this? You're still mulling that over?

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.230
Like I said before. There is no meaning to this world.

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:02.320
I understand that logic with my head.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:05.010
But there must've been a reason for what happened.

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:07.490
A reason why I was made to relive a time again.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:09.660
There is evidence of an infiltration of this ship.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.470
There is a distinct possibility that there is an alien onboard.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.320
All stations, remain in the highest state of alert.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:15.720
Thinking about it,
All stations, remain in the highest state of alert.

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.240
Thinking about it,

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:16.480
All crew, avoid being alone and follow the instructions of security.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:20.230
we don't know anything about Jovian Lizards.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:21.910
Historically, humanity has not established colonies beyond Mars.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:22.780
Repeat...

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.740
Historically, humanity has not established colonies beyond Mars.

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:27.760
There's no chance that the Jovian Lizards could be humans.

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:30.810
Can't he hide his enthusiasm at all?

00:13:32.550 --> 00:13:33.590
Oh, yes!

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:34.240
You're not going to the bridge?

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:35.070
Stay still!

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:35.580
You're not going to the bridge?

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:36.770
Everyone's being called out.

00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:40.010
Oh, I wanted to tidy up here first.

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:40.690
Do you want me to help?

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:42.810
Aquamarine!

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:44.530
Oh, no!

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.120
Aquamarine...

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:47.990
Who's this?

00:13:50.990 --> 00:13:52.180
Please excuse me.

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:54.840
I'm part of the states of Ganymede, Callisto, and Europa's

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.230
Anti-Earth Cooperative Federation of the Jovian Realm,

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.050
from the Space Assault Superior Male Forces,

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:01.290
Lieutenant Commander Shiratori Tsukumo.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:02.530
Japanese?

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:06.710
Our nation has prospered near Jupiter for the last hundred years.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.530
Wait a minute, haven't you read a history book in school?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.140
The people of Earth have only built colonies on Mars so far.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:15.060
That is the history of your people.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:18.930
Security here. Is something the matter here?

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:19.920
Nothing here.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.420
Everyone needs to assemble at the bridge or the cafeteria.

00:14:22.680 --> 00:14:24.360
All right, thank you!

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:29.240
Is this all right, Haruka-san? Goat-san is sure to get angry.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.990
I can stand sticking my neck out for an injured person.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.660
And you know, I want to hear what he has to say.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.660
Let's hurry to a safe location.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.330
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.220
An emergency security alert is in effect!

00:14:43.220 --> 00:14:45.270
Why do I get the feeling that you're enjoying this?

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:46.840
Hunting down and cornering a person?

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:48.760
I'm saying that you're in harm's way.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.880
Don't you have the balls to order me around? Say, to my death?!

00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:56.440
Women are the treasures of a nation!

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:57.780
And you claim to be a soldier, you bastard!

00:14:58.190 --> 00:14:59.630
You're under arrest! Give yourself up!

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:01.020
You're under arrest!

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:13.570
Did you dream again? Was it the same dream?

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:14.560
Yeah...

00:15:15.100 --> 00:15:17.240
Oh man, I'm like a kid.

00:15:17.900 --> 00:15:19.370
Why do I see that dream over and over?

00:15:19.710 --> 00:15:22.040
That illustrious castle that glitters, right?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:27.090
Maybe you're the reincarnation of a warrior of an ancient civilization.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:28.210
What's that about?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.960
Well, that's the only explanation that makes sense.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.770
I mean, you became the Nadesico's ace pilot without having any training.

00:15:33.770 --> 00:15:35.440
You can teleport all by yourself.

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:36.890
You're probably different from people in some way.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:39.720
I'm nothing like that. Just...

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:42.390
What's that?!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.790
Damn invaders!

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.070
We will not have you build any more of your demonic weapons to use against us!

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.480
Daimajin Tornado!

00:15:58.110 --> 00:15:59.270
You're a godsend.

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:03.230
Please take care of it before the UEAF reinforcements arrive.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:04.290
Why?

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.370
That's the reason.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.970
Nadesico Class vessel number four, Shakuyaku.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:11.300
We've been building her in secret as part of our plan to campaign on Mars.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:14.390
Is Nergal deceiving the military again?

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.690
Please, we need you to pull this one off.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:20.030
I'm not interested in this ship or Mars anymore.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.220
I just can't forgive the Jovian Lizards!

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:26.140
I can't forgive myself for turning away from fighting them either!

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.560
Behold, the might of justice!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:41.280
Evil humanoid weapon! Let's go, Daimajin!

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:42.910
Gekigan Beam!

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:46.970
Bastard! He's the same type as the one that appeared on Earth!

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:52.160
The lunar frame is a self-contained unit with a phase transition engine onboard,

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:53.630
but its reaction time is much slower.

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:54.800
Fire the rail gun at close range for effect!

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:56.420
I got it!

00:16:56.420 --> 00:16:59.550
There isn't any way I'm going to let that thing fire a gravity blast!

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.190
This is hard to believe, but he is certainly a human from Earth.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:10.110
While there are signs that his DNA was slightly modified...

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:11.530
Don't call me an Earthling!

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.690
I am a proud soldier of the Jovian Federation.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:16.850
Captain, we are on a landing approach to the Moon.

00:17:17.180 --> 00:17:21.700
Currently a Nergal Aestivalis is engaging an enemy Goliath type.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:25.010
Really? I wonder if Akito is all right?

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:26.920
Well then, I'll head to the bridge right now.

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:27.790
If you would...

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:29.880
What of the prisoner and the two who aided him?!

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:33.300
Saving Akito's life is more important than bullying Megumi and Minato!

00:17:33.660 --> 00:17:35.210
Are you sure, Captain?

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.110
Of course, this isn't all right!

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:40.270
This is not a matter between a man and a woman. This is war!

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:43.720
But we are men and women.

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:49.020
The Captain is just too soft.

00:17:49.730 --> 00:17:51.280
I think this is far enough.

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.830
It's better if the Jovian Lizards are assumed to be

00:17:56.830 --> 00:17:58.340
a mysterious army of unmanned weapons.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:00.530
Just when everyone is starting to get pumped up about all this,

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:02.360
your timing is horrible...

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:03.950
Ouch...

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.040
Run!

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:11.140
But I'm a captured prisoner, so...

00:18:11.960 --> 00:18:13.190
No excuses!

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.330
This is your only chance!

00:18:15.330 --> 00:18:16.210
You two!

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:17.630
What have you done?!

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:21.290
I'm sorry!

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:24.390
Damn it!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:25.530
Here I go.

00:18:25.780 --> 00:18:27.350
Gekigan Shoot!

00:18:36.410 --> 00:18:37.490
No!

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:41.920
That's where all the helpless people are!

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.040
You'll pay for this! Trashing my Daimajin!

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:54.330
What? Who the hell are you?!

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:57.630
You'll never extinguish the flame of justice burning brightly within my soul.

00:18:58.080 --> 00:18:59.420
I will protect my nation!

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:01.630
Even if it means I perish in the process!

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:05.050
You? You're a Jovian Lizard?

00:19:05.730 --> 00:19:07.470
Akito? It really is you, Akito!

00:19:08.140 --> 00:19:10.140
Answer me! Who the hell are you?!

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:11.500
We might have been...

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.460
We might have been friends if we were born on different planets than we were.

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.930
Hey, Akito, we'll be right there, so hold on!

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:20.040
Be quiet!

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:22.540
What? Reinforcements?! What treachery!

00:19:22.540 --> 00:19:25.380
Damn you! I will surely defeat you when next we meet!

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:26.950
Hey, wait!

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:37.260
Human? They're humans?

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:39.460
That's impossible!

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:43.330
This is the consequence of your methodology, Captain.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:44.970
Our prisoner escaped,

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:48.140
and Helmswoman Haruka and Communications Officer Reinard are missing.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:50.060
Jun-kun...

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:52.850
This just means that the enemy is the enemy, Yurika.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:55.350
You can't fight with your emotions alone guiding you.

00:19:55.910 --> 00:19:56.690
Jun-kun...

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.960
Hunting down your friends isn't anything pleasant to do.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:05.650
I'll come along too! This was my fault!

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:06.720
Hey, wait a minute.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.560
An enemy prisoner got away?

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.260
Akito, you're all right? Thank heavens!

00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:13.440
You should rest after that.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:17.440
I thought I was doing my best to do the right thing,

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:17.780
but maybe I was wrong.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:18.940
I won't allow this,

00:20:19.260 --> 00:20:19.380
But this is the only way I can think of doing things.

00:20:19.380 --> 00:20:21.800
being human like us.

00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:21.820
But this is the only way I can think of doing things.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:22.050
You understand what I'm talking about, right, Akito?

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:22.340
This can't be real.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:23.840
You understand what I'm talking about, right, Akito?

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.520
Shut up already!

00:20:25.520 --> 00:20:28.020
Hinagiku, taking off to pursue the escaped prisoner!

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:37.770
What's wrong, Akito?

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.090
Something's different about you. You're scaring me.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:49.940
Xebec Studio Newsletter! peep pipi peep peep...

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:52.050
And so, here we are at Xebec, which makes Nadesico.

00:21:52.190 --> 00:21:53.890
Hey, there's someone sleeping under his desk.

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:55.800
Time now to talk to the director!

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:57.430
Uh, hello. I'm Sato the director.

00:21:57.430 --> 00:21:59.290
In the next episode, Yurika will work hard like a good captain should.

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.410
Oh really? I'm ecstatic!

00:22:00.410 --> 00:22:00.860
What's wrong with you?!
Oh really? I'm ecstatic!

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:01.150
What's wrong with you?!

00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:02.430
What's all that on your back?

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:03.520
They gave me cels from Gekiganger.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:04.250
I see.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.870
Next Martian Successor Nadesico: "The Beginning of Nadesico's War"

00:22:07.870 --> 00:22:09.360
Oh! Let's watch it, everyone!

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:10.570
It's a promise! OK?
